<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44284" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">silvesco</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sylv-</span></b> ), ĕre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch. n.</i> [id.], of the
			grape-vine, <i>to grow</i> or <i>run
			wild</i>, <i>to run to wood</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(vitis) ne silvescat sarmentis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Sen. 15, 52</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nec pati vitem silvescere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					4, 11, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">capilli silvescentium crinium velleribus
					involuti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 3, p. 109</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
